                <pb facs="0808" n="696" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg696"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13278: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Josselyn</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-14T18:00:00+08:00">November 14, 1935—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received—8:33 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>59. My November 14, 4 p.m. Adventist Mission Tatsienlu telegraphs November 14
                    that situation still serious and east and south roads blocked. Repeated to
                    Peiping, Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josselyn</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
